e Joker are my trump cards.\n\nSo, ♠K it is.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: The Landlord (Next Player) played a single Q, beating my teammate\'s J. As the player acting immediately before the Landlord (Gatekeeper position), my role is to block the Landlord from winning tricks with medium-strength cards and to force them to spend high value cards (A, 2, Jokers). My teammate passed, signaling they cannot or do not want to beat the Q. I have a strong hand with the Red Joker and three 2s, plus K and A as high singles. Playing the King is the most efficient move; it beats the Queen without wasting my top control cards (2s or Joker) or breaking my triplet of 2s, and it forces the Landlord to either pass or use an Ace/2/Joker to proceed.\n\nReason: I need to block the Landlord\'s Q to prevent them from maintaining control cheaply. ♠K is the lowest single card in my hand that beats ♠Q. Playing it puts pressure on the Landlord to use a higher card (like an Ace or 2), which benefits the Peasant team by exhausting the Landlord\'s resources. Passing is passive and allows the Landlord to dictate the flow.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠K"]}'}
